I have a complete picture of the owner-identity implementation. Here is my report.

## Package structure & naming conventions

The app is a Spring PetClinic variant driven through a single OfficeFloor pipeline for `POST /api/owners`. Base package: `org.springframework.samples.petclinic`.

- `model/` — JPA entities (`Owner`, `Person`, `BaseEntity`, ...).
- `rest/function/owner/` — one class per pipeline step (verbs like `AssignOwnerCustomerCode`) plus pure helper/value classes (nouns like `CustomerCode`, `Luhn`, `Locality`, `Postcode`, `SameCity`). Helpers are `final` with a private constructor and static methods; each is documented as "the single definition of ...".
- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — MapStruct mapper that computes read-only derived DTO fields via `default` methods.
- `rest/escalation/` — exception + handler pairs.
- Pipeline wiring (step order) lives in `src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`; the DTO contract is in `src/main/resources/openapi.yml`.

The create pipeline order (from `owners.POST.yml`): validate → ensurePostcode → normalize(tel/email/address) → ensureCityCapacity → ensureDailyLimit → build → assignHousehold → ensureUniqueIdentity → resolveRegistrationDate → **assignCustomerCode** → countNamesakes → assignMembershipLevel → save → **audit** → respond.

## 1. customerCode construction

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CustomerCode.java` — the format definition. Current format is `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`:
```java
25  static String format(String city, String lastName, int sequence) {
26      return String.format("%s-%s-%04d", prefix(city), prefix(lastName), sequence);
27  }
30  private static String prefix(String value) {
31      return value.substring(0, Math.min(PREFIX_LENGTH, value.length())).toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT);
32  }
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java` — the pipeline step that assigns it, deriving the sequence from same-city owners:
```java
18  public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
19      int sequence = SameCity.count(ownerRepository.findAll(), owner.getCity()) + 1;
20      owner.setCustomerCode(CustomerCode.format(owner.getCity(), owner.getLastName(), sequence));
21  }
```

Note a documentation/impl mismatch: the code produces `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (e.g. `SPR-SMI-0007`), but `openapi.yml` (lines 2100-2107) documents customerCode as `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` (example `SMI-0007`), and the membershipNumber example there is `SMI-0007-M26`.

## 2. membership number & check digit (both computed from customerCode)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java` — derived on read in the mapper:
```java
27  @Mapping(target = "membershipNumber", expression = "java(membershipNumber(owner))")
28  @Mapping(target = "checkDigit", expression = "java(checkDigit(owner))")
29  @Mapping(target = "locality", expression = "java(locality(owner))")
...
56  default String membershipNumber(Owner owner) {
57      String customerCode = owner.getCustomerCode();
58      LocalDate registrationDate = owner.getRegistrationDate();
59      if (customerCode == null || registrationDate == null) {
60          return null;
61      }
62      return String.format("%s-M%02d", customerCode, registrationDate.getYear() % 100);
63  }
67  default Integer checkDigit(Owner owner) {
68      String customerCode = owner.getCustomerCode();
69      return customerCode == null ? null : Luhn.checkDigit(customerCode);
70  }
```

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/Luhn.java` — the check-digit algorithm (ignores non-digits, so it runs over the whole formatted customerCode):
```java
17  public static int checkDigit(String value) {
18      int sum = 0;
19      boolean doubled = true;
20      for (int i = value.length() - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
21          char c = value.charAt(i);
22          if (c < '0' || c > '9') { continue; }
23          int digit = c - '0';
24          if (doubled) { digit *= 2; if (digit > 9) { digit -= 9; } }
32          sum += digit;
33          doubled = !doubled;
34      }
35      return (10 - (sum % 10)) % 10;
36  }
```

Note: membershipNumber/checkDigit are derived from `customerCode`, so any change to customerCode format flows into them automatically. membershipNumber also depends on `registrationDate` (set by `ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate`).

## 3. locality derivation (from postcode/city)

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/Locality.java` — postcode-first, then city table, else `UNKNOWN`:
```java
20  private static final Map<String, String> CITY_REGION =
21          Map.of("Sydney", "NSW", "Melbourne", "VIC", "Brisbane", "QLD");
28  public static String region(String city) {
29      return CITY_REGION.getOrDefault(city, UNKNOWN);
30  }
34  public static String region(String city, String postcode) {
35      String byPostcode = Postcode.region(postcode);
36      return byPostcode != null ? byPostcode : region(city);
37  }
```
Consumed in `OwnerMapper.locality()` (line 75-76). It derives from `city` and `postcode` — not from the customerCode.

## 4. region code from postcode

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/Postcode.java` — fixed region→range table and reverse lookup:
```java
16  private static final Map<String, int[]> REGION_RANGE =
17          Map.of("NSW", new int[] {2000, 2099}, "VIC", new int[] {3000, 3099},
18                  "QLD", new int[] {4000, 4099});
43  public static String region(String postcode) {
44      if (!isWellFormed(postcode)) { return null; }
47      int value = Integer.parseInt(postcode);
48      for (Map.Entry<String, int[]> entry : REGION_RANGE.entrySet()) {
49          int[] range = entry.getValue();
50          if (value >= range[0] && value <= range[1]) { return entry.getKey(); }
53      }
54      return null;
55  }
```
Also `isWellFormed` (4-digit regex) and `isInRegion(city, postcode)` for validation.

## 5. create audit record using customerCode

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java` — runs after save, logs one line to the `AUDIT` logger including customerCode:
```java
17  private static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT");
19  public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
20      AUDIT.info("Owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={}",
21              owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(), owner.getMembershipLevel());
22  }
```
Audit is captured in tests via `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java` (a Logback `ListAppender` on the `AUDIT` logger).

## 6. sequence-number logic / counters

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/SameCity.java` — the per-city counter that feeds the sequence:
```java
20  static boolean matches(Owner owner, String city) {
21      return normalize(owner.getCity()).equals(normalize(city));
22  }
25  static int count(Iterable<Owner> owners, String city) {
26      int inCity = 0;
27      for (Owner owner : owners) { if (matches(owner, city)) { inCity++; } }
32      return inCity;
33  }
36  private static String normalize(String value) {
37      return value == null ? "" : value.strip().toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
38  }
```
The sequence is `count(...) + 1` computed in `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` (line 19). It is currently per-city, whereas openapi.yml describes it as a "global 4-digit ... sequence" — another doc/impl discrepancy. There is no persisted counter/DB sequence; it is recomputed from `ownerRepository.findAll()` on each create.

## 7. existing tests

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java` — a single failing/target test expecting a NEW format `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (not the current `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`):
```java
7   /** global-id: Redesign owner identity. The customerCode must become '<REGION>-<HASH8>' where REGION is t... */
11  void coreCustomerCodeIsRegionHash() throws Exception {
12      int id = createOwnerOk(withPostcode(ownerNode()));
13      JsonNode n = fetchOwner(id);
14      assertTrue(n.get("customerCode").asText().matches("[A-Z0-9]+-[0-9A-F]{8}")); // <REGION>-<HASH8>
